+**Every mutating command below runs through the locked CLI** —
+`python3 scripts/access-mutate.py <subcommand> ...`, from the repo root. This
+goes through the same locked read-modify-write transaction every access.json
+writer uses (`access_store.mutate_access_file`) — do NOT read access.json and
+write it back by hand; a freehand edit races the bridge's own writers
+(tier-map seeding, thread-engage seeding, pairing) and can silently drop one
+side's update. Each subcommand prints a JSON result on stdout: report its
+`ok`/error/added/removed/skipped fields to the user. A non-zero exit or an
+`"ok": false` result means the target didn't exist or access.json was
+unreadable — relay the `error` field, don't retry by hand.
