 ### `pair <code>`
 
-1. Read `~/.claude/channels/discord/access.json`.
-2. Look up `pending[<code>]`. If not found or `expiresAt < Date.now()`,
-   tell the user and stop.
-3. Extract `senderId` and `chatId` from the pending entry.
-4. Add `senderId` to `allowFrom` (dedupe).
-5. Delete `pending[<code>]`.
-6. Write the updated access.json.
-7. `mkdir -p ~/.claude/channels/discord/approved` then write
-   `~/.claude/channels/discord/approved/<senderId>` with `chatId` as the
-   file contents. The channel server polls this dir and sends "you're in".
-8. Confirm: who was approved (senderId).
+```
+python3 scripts/access-mutate.py pair <code>
+```
+Looks up `pending[<code>]` (stopping if not found or expired), adds its
+`senderId` to `allowFrom`, deletes the pending entry, and — only after that
+locked write succeeds — writes the per-sender approved marker (see "State
+shape" above for the exact path) with `chatId` as the contents (the channel
+server polls this dir and sends "you're in"). Confirm to the user who was
+approved (`senderId`).
 
 ### `deny <code>`
 
-1. Read access.json, delete `pending[<code>]`, write back.
-2. Confirm.
+```
+python3 scripts/access-mutate.py deny <code>
+```
+Deletes `pending[<code>]`. Confirm.
 
 ### `allow <senderId>`
 
-1. Read access.json (create default if missing).
-2. Add `<senderId>` to `allowFrom` (dedupe).
-3. Write back.
+```
+python3 scripts/access-mutate.py allow <senderId>
+```
+Adds `<senderId>` to `allowFrom` (dedupe).
 
 ### `remove <senderId>`
 
-1. Read, filter `allowFrom` to exclude `<senderId>`, write.
+```
+python3 scripts/access-mutate.py remove <senderId>
+```
+Filters `<senderId>` out of `allowFrom`.
 
 ### `policy <mode>`
 
-1. Validate `<mode>` is one of `pairing`, `allowlist`, `disabled`.
-2. Read (create default if missing), set `dmPolicy`, write.
+```
+python3 scripts/access-mutate.py policy <mode>
+```
+`<mode>` must be one of `pairing`, `allowlist`, `disabled` — validate before
+invoking; the CLI rejects anything else.
 
 ### `group add <channelId>` (optional: `--no-mention`, `--allow id1,id2`)
 
-1. Read (create default if missing).
-2. Set `groups[<channelId>] = { requireMention: !hasFlag("--no-mention"),
-   allowFrom: parsedAllowList }`.
-3. Write.
+```
+python3 scripts/access-mutate.py group-add <channelId> [--no-mention] [--allow id1,id2]
+```
+Sets `groups[<channelId>] = { requireMention: !hasFlag("--no-mention"),
+allowFrom: parsedAllowList }`, **replacing** any existing entry for that
+channel. Use `group append` instead when the goal is adding to an existing
+group without dropping current members.
 
 ### `group rm <channelId>`
 
-1. Read, `delete groups[<channelId>]`, write.
+```
+python3 scripts/access-mutate.py group-rm <channelId>
+```
+Deletes `groups[<channelId>]`.
 
